\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. It is a thing most wonderful,
\par Almost too wonderful to be,
\par That God's own Son should come from heaven,
\par And die to save a child like me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And yet I know that it is true;
\par He chose a poor and humble lot,
\par And wept and toiled and mourned and died,
\par For love of those who loved Him not.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I sometime think about the Cross,
\par And shut my eyes and try to see
\par The cruel nails and crown of thorns,
\par And Jesus crucified for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. But even could I see Him die,
\par I could but see a little part
\par Of that great love which like a fire
\par Is always burning in His heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I cannot tell how He could love
\par A child so weak and full of love;
\par His love must be most wonderful,
\par If He could die my love to win.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. It is most wonderful to know
\par His love for me so free and sure;
\par But 'tis more wonderful to see
\par My love for Him so faint and poor.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. And yet I want to love Thee, Lord;
\par O light the flame within my heart,
\par And I will love Thee more and more,
\par Until I see Thee as Thou art.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

